nodecode-deepsec is a rewrite of Unclecheng-li's Unclecheng-li/DeepSec:

  https://github.com/Unclecheng-li/DeepSec
  commit fff031fc01fb36b95348214c8ee359f6ede8aa8b

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 VibeGuard contributors (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's four model tools -- deepsec_scan, deepsec_agent_audit,
deepsec_supply_chain and deepsec_report -- with the finding shape they answered (rule,
severity, title, target, line, evidence, suggestion, layer), their severity summary,
the saved-result JSON a report renders, and the three settings that steered them (how
many findings an answer carries, whether test folders are read, and the severity floor).
The rules and the file walk behind them are Common Lisp here, where the original shelled
out to its own Python CLI.

Left out: the original CLI's Tree-sitter AST layer and its optional LLM review of source,
which needed that CLI and a provider key; the signed-scope penetration-testing lane the
same repository ships as a sibling plugin; and the CLI's own report templates and
attack-chain page, replaced by markdown, json, sarif and text renderers. The rewrite reads
files, never runs them, and dials nothing.
